---
/*
 * PlannerReportingPathSelector.astro
 *
 * Purpose:
 * Helps readers choose a practical Planner reporting path based on the
 * planner model and reporting requirement.
 *
 * Source-aligned choices:
 *   Standard / Basic → Excel, Power Automate, or Microsoft Graph
 *   Premium         → Project Power BI template, Dataverse + Power BI,
 *                      or Dataverse → Fabric / OneLake → Power BI
 *
 * This is an architecture decision aid, not a licensing calculator or
 * Microsoft-prescribed decision engine.
 */
---

<section
  class="prps"
  data-prps
  aria-labelledby="prps-title"
>
  <div class="prps__header">
    <div>
      <p class="prps__eyebrow">Reporting path selector</p>

      <h3 id="prps-title">
        Which Planner reporting path fits the requirement?
      </h3>

      <p class="prps__intro">
        Start with the plan type, then classify how the report will be used.
        The selector recommends a practical path and the design concerns to
        review before implementation.
      </p>
    </div>

    <span
      class="prps__badge"
      data-badge
      aria-live="polite"
    >
      Choose a plan type
    </span>
  </div>

  <fieldset class="prps__questions">
    <legend>Classify the reporting requirement</legend>

    <div class="prps__question prps__question--wide">
      <span class="prps__question-title">
        1. Which Planner model are you reporting from?
      </span>

      <div class="prps__options">
        <label>
          <input
            type="radio"
            name="prps-plan-type"
            value="standard"
          />
          <span>Planner Standard / Basic</span>
        </label>

        <label>
          <input
            type="radio"
            name="prps-plan-type"
            value="premium"
          />
          <span>Planner Premium</span>
        </label>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="prps__question">
      <span class="prps__question-title">
        2. What is the primary reporting need?
      </span>

      <div class="prps__options">
        <label>
          <input
            type="radio"
            name="prps-use-case"
            value="adhoc"
          />
          <span>Ad hoc / departmental</span>
        </label>

        <label>
          <input
            type="radio"
            name="prps-use-case"
            value="operational"
          />
          <span>Recurring operational</span>
        </label>

        <label>
          <input
            type="radio"
            name="prps-use-case"
            value="portfolio"
          />
          <span>Portfolio / project</span>
        </label>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="prps__question">
      <span class="prps__question-title">
        3. How broad is the reporting scope?
      </span>

      <div class="prps__options">
        <label>
          <input
            type="radio"
            name="prps-scope"
            value="single"
          />
          <span>Single plan</span>
        </label>

        <label>
          <input
            type="radio"
            name="prps-scope"
            value="multi"
          />
          <span>Multiple plans</span>
        </label>

        <label>
          <input
            type="radio"
            name="prps-scope"
            value="enterprise"
          />
          <span>Cross-system / enterprise</span>
        </label>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="prps__question">
      <span class="prps__question-title">
        4. Do you need richer project-management information?
      </span>

      <div class="prps__options">
        <label>
          <input
            type="radio"
            name="prps-project-data"
            value="no"
          />
          <span>No</span>
        </label>

        <label>
          <input
            type="radio"
            name="prps-project-data"
            value="yes"
          />
          <span>Yes</span>
        </label>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="prps__question">
      <span class="prps__question-title">
        5. Do you need a broader analytical layer?
      </span>

      <div class="prps__options">
        <label>
          <input
            type="radio"
            name="prps-analytics"
            value="no"
          />
          <span>No</span>
        </label>

        <label>
          <input
            type="radio"
            name="prps-analytics"
            value="yes"
          />
          <span>Yes</span>
        </label>
      </div>
    </div>
  </fieldset>

  <div
    class="prps__result"
    aria-live="polite"
    aria-atomic="true"
  >
    <div class="prps__result-head">
      <div>
        <span class="prps__result-kicker">
          Recommended reporting path
        </span>

        <h4 data-title>
          Complete the classification.
        </h4>
      </div>

      <span
        class="prps__result-level"
        data-level
      >
        Awaiting input
      </span>
    </div>

    <p
      class="prps__result-description"
      data-description
    >
      The selector will identify the reporting path that best matches the
      selected Planner model and reporting requirement.
    </p>

    <div class="prps__meter" aria-hidden="true">
      <span data-meter></span>
    </div>

    <div class="prps__cards">
      <div class="prps__card">
        <span>Recommended path</span>
        <strong data-path>—</strong>
      </div>

      <div class="prps__card">
        <span>Best fit</span>
        <strong data-fit>—</strong>
      </div>

      <div class="prps__card">
        <span>Review next</span>
        <strong data-review>—</strong>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="prps__principle">
    <span
      class="prps__principle-mark"
      aria-hidden="true"
    >
      →
    </span>

    <p>
      <strong>Choose the simplest supported path that meets the reporting need.</strong>
      Standard reporting generally needs an extraction step; Premium reporting can
      start from its Dataverse-backed project data.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<script>
  const roots = document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>(
    "[data-prps]"
  );

  roots.forEach((root) => {
    if (root.dataset.initialized === "true") {
      return;
    }

    root.dataset.initialized = "true";

    const badge =
      root.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-badge]");

    const title =
      root.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-title]");

    const level =
      root.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-level]");

    const description =
      root.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-description]");

    const meter =
      root.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-meter]");

    const path =
      root.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-path]");

    const fit =
      root.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-fit]");

    const review =
      root.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-review]");

    if (
      !badge ||
      !title ||
      !level ||
      !description ||
      !meter ||
      !path ||
      !fit ||
      !review
    ) {
      return;
    }

    const getValue = (name: string) =>
      root.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>(
        `input[name="${name}"]:checked`
      )?.value;

    function setIncomplete(selected: number) {
      root.dataset.state = "incomplete";

      badge.textContent = "COMPLETE CLASSIFICATION";
      title.textContent = `${selected} of 5 areas classified`;
      level.textContent = `${5 - selected} remaining`;

      description.textContent =
        "Complete the classification to receive a reporting-path recommendation.";

      meter.style.width =
        `${Math.round((selected / 5) * 100)}%`;

      path.textContent = "Complete the classification";
      fit.textContent = "Complete the classification";
      review.textContent = "Complete the classification";
    }

    function setResult(
      state: string,
      badgeText: string,
      levelText: string,
      resultTitle: string,
      resultDescription: string,
      resultPath: string,
      resultFit: string,
      resultReview: string,
      width: string
    ) {
      root.dataset.state = state;

      badge.textContent = badgeText;
      level.textContent = levelText;
      title.textContent = resultTitle;
      description.textContent = resultDescription;
      path.textContent = resultPath;
      fit.textContent = resultFit;
      review.textContent = resultReview;
      meter.style.width = width;
    }

    function updateAssessment() {
      const planType = getValue("prps-plan-type");
      const useCase = getValue("prps-use-case");
      const scope = getValue("prps-scope");
      const projectData = getValue("prps-project-data");
      const analytics = getValue("prps-analytics");

      const selected = [
        planType,
        useCase,
        scope,
        projectData,
        analytics
      ].filter(Boolean).length;

      if (selected < 5) {
        setIncomplete(selected);
        return;
      }

      /*
       * Standard / Basic:
       *   - Excel → ad hoc analysis
       *   - Power Automate → low-code recurring extraction
       *   - Microsoft Graph → automated multi-plan reporting
       *
       * Premium:
       *   - Project Power BI template → fast portfolio reporting
       *   - Dataverse + Power BI → custom analytical model
       *   - Dataverse → Fabric / OneLake → Power BI → enterprise analytics
       */

      if (planType === "standard") {
        if (scope === "enterprise") {
          setResult(
            "standard-graph",
            "STANDARD / GRAPH",
            "Automated extraction",
            "Use Microsoft Graph with a durable reporting layer.",
            "The requirement is broader than a lightweight plan report, so a programmatic extraction path provides more control than manual export.",
            "Planner Standard → Microsoft Graph → Reporting Store → Power BI",
            "Automated multi-plan or broader Standard reporting.",
            "Graph permissions, pagination, persistence, refresh, security, and API/service limits.",
            "85%"
          );
          return;
        }

        if (useCase === "adhoc" || scope === "single") {
          setResult(
            "standard-excel",
            "STANDARD / EXCEL",
            "Lightweight reporting",
            "Use Excel export for simple, ad hoc analysis.",
            "The requirement is lightweight enough that a manual export can be a practical starting point.",
            "Planner Standard → Excel → Power BI / analysis",
            "One-off or departmental reporting with limited governance needs.",
            "File storage, replacement/refresh behavior, and the point at which the report needs an automated path.",
            "45%"
          );
          return;
        }

        setResult(
          "standard-automate",
          "STANDARD / AUTOMATE",
          "Low-code recurring",
          "Use Power Automate for recurring extraction into a reporting store.",
          "A recurring Standard-plan report benefits from low-code orchestration without requiring a full custom API extraction service.",
          "Planner Standard → Power Automate → Reporting Store → Power BI",
          "Recurring, low-code operational reporting.",
          "Connector scope, throttling, durable storage, refresh, credentials, and flow ownership.",
          "65%"
        );

        return;
      }

      /*
       * Premium recommendations.
       * The enterprise path wins when a separate analytical layer is explicitly
       * required, the reporting spans systems, or enterprise-scale analytics
       * is the stated requirement.
       */
      if (analytics === "yes" || scope === "enterprise") {
        setResult(
          "premium-fabric",
          "PREMIUM / FABRIC",
          "Enterprise analytics",
          "Use Dataverse as the source and add Fabric / OneLake for broader analytics.",
          "The requirement calls for a broader analytical layer, cross-system reporting, or enterprise-scale reuse.",
          "Planner Premium → Dataverse → Fabric / OneLake → Power BI",
          "Cross-system, reusable, or enterprise analytical reporting.",
          "Data engineering, conformed models, history, governance, capacity, security, and operational ownership.",
          "100%"
        );
        return;
      }

      if (useCase === "portfolio" || projectData === "yes") {
        setResult(
          "premium-dataverse",
          "PREMIUM / DATAVERSE",
          "Project analytics",
          "Use Dataverse with Power BI for custom project analytics.",
          "The reporting need depends on richer project information such as schedules, dependencies, milestones, resources, or custom fields.",
          "Planner Premium → Dataverse → Power BI",
          "Custom project or portfolio analytics.",
          "Dataverse permissions, semantic-model design, KPI definitions, security, refresh, and performance.",
          "78%"
        );
        return;
      }

      setResult(
        "premium-template",
        "PREMIUM / TEMPLATE",
        "Fast starting point",
        "Start with the Microsoft Project Power BI template.",
        "The requirement is project-oriented but does not yet indicate a need for a broader custom analytical platform.",
        "Planner Premium → Project Power BI template → Power BI",
        "Fast portfolio-style reporting and initial exploration.",
        "Template fit, current licensing, customization needs, and transition to a governed custom model.",
        "60%"
      );
    }

    root
      .querySelectorAll<HTMLInputElement>(
        '.prps__options input[type="radio"]'
      )
      .forEach((input) => {
        input.addEventListener("change", updateAssessment);
      });

    updateAssessment();
  });
</script>

<style>
  .prps {
    --prps-surface: var(--surface-primary, #ffffff);
    --prps-surface-soft: var(--surface-secondary, #f8fafc);
    --prps-text: var(--text-primary, #0f172a);
    --prps-text-secondary: var(--text-secondary, #475569);
    --prps-text-tertiary: var(--text-tertiary, #64748b);
    --prps-border: var(--border-default, #dbe3ec);
    --prps-border-soft: var(--border-subtle, #e7edf4);
    --prps-accent: var(--color-accent, #4ea1e0);
    --prps-state: var(--prps-accent);

    width: 100%;
    margin-block: var(--space-10, 2.5rem);
    padding: clamp(1.25rem, 3vw, 2rem);
    color: var(--prps-text);
    background: var(--prps-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--prps-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg, 0.875rem);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm, 0 1px 2px rgb(15 23 42 / 0.06));
  }

  .prps[data-state="standard-excel"] {
    --prps-state: #b45309;
  }

  .prps[data-state="standard-automate"] {
    --prps-state: #2563eb;
  }

  .prps[data-state="standard-graph"] {
    --prps-state: #1d4ed8;
  }

  .prps[data-state="premium-template"] {
    --prps-state: #15803d;
  }

  .prps[data-state="premium-dataverse"] {
    --prps-state: #0f766e;
  }

  .prps[data-state="premium-fabric"] {
    --prps-state: #7c3aed;
  }

  .prps__header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--space-6, 1.5rem);
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .prps__eyebrow {
    margin: 0 0 0.3rem;
    color: var(--prps-state);
    font-size: var(--font-size-xs, 0.75rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .prps h3,
  .prps h4,
  .prps p {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .prps h3 {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    font-size: clamp(1.3rem, 2vw, 1.6rem);
    line-height: 1.2;
  }

  .prps__intro {
    max-width: 74ch;
    margin-bottom: 0;
    color: var(--prps-text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .prps__badge {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    align-self: flex-start;
    padding: 0.45rem 0.75rem;
    color: var(--prps-state);
    background: color-mix(
      in srgb,
      var(--prps-state) 8%,
      var(--prps-surface)
    );
    border: 1px solid color-mix(
      in srgb,
      var(--prps-state) 30%,
      var(--prps-border)
    );
    border-radius: 999px;
    font-size: var(--font-size-xs, 0.75rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .prps__questions {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 0.85rem;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    border: 0;
  }

  .prps__questions legend {
    width: 100%;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--prps-text);
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm, 0.875rem);
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .prps__question--wide {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
  }

  .prps__question {
    padding: 1rem;
    background: var(--prps-surface-soft);
    border: 1px solid var(--prps-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md, 0.65rem);
  }

  .prps__question-title {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--prps-text);
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm, 0.875rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.45;
  }

  .prps__options {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }

  .prps__options label {
    position: relative;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .prps__options input {
    position: absolute;
    width: 1px;
    height: 1px;
    opacity: 0;
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .prps__options label span {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    min-height: 2.25rem;
    padding: 0.45rem 0.8rem;
    color: var(--prps-text-secondary);
    background: var(--prps-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--prps-border);
    border-radius: 999px;
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm, 0.875rem);
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.35;
    transition:
      border-color 160ms ease,
      background-color 160ms ease,
      color 160ms ease;
  }

  .prps__options label:hover span {
    border-color: var(--prps-accent);
  }

  .prps__options label:has(input:focus-visible) span {
    outline: 2px solid var(--prps-accent);
    outline-offset: 2px;
  }

  .prps__options label:has(input:checked) span {
    color: var(--prps-state);
    background: color-mix(
      in srgb,
      var(--prps-state) 8%,
      var(--prps-surface)
    );
    border-color: var(--prps-state);
  }

  .prps__result {
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
    padding: 1.2rem;
    background: var(--prps-surface-soft);
    border: 1px solid var(--prps-border);
    border-left: 4px solid var(--prps-state);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md, 0.65rem);
  }

  .prps__result-head {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .prps__result-kicker {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
    color: var(--prps-text-tertiary);
    font-size: var(--font-size-xs, 0.75rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .prps__result h4 {
    margin-bottom: 0;
    color: var(--prps-text);
    font-size: var(--font-size-lg, 1.1rem);
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .prps__result-level {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    color: var(--prps-state);
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm, 0.875rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    text-align: right;
  }

  .prps__result-description {
    max-width: 74ch;
    margin: 0.65rem 0 0;
    color: var(--prps-text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .prps__meter {
    width: 100%;
    height: 0.45rem;
    margin-top: 1rem;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: var(--prps-border-soft);
    border-radius: 999px;
  }

  .prps__meter span {
    display: block;
    width: 0;
    height: 100%;
    background: var(--prps-state);
    border-radius: inherit;
    transition:
      width 180ms ease,
      background-color 180ms ease;
  }

  .prps__cards {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .prps__card {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.35rem;
    padding: 0.9rem;
    background: var(--prps-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--prps-border-soft);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm, 0.5rem);
  }

  .prps__card span {
    color: var(--prps-text-tertiary);
    font-size: var(--font-size-xs, 0.75rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .prps__card strong {
    color: var(--prps-text-secondary);
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm, 0.875rem);
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .prps__principle {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin-top: 1rem;
    padding: 0.9rem 1rem;
    background: var(--prps-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--prps-border-soft);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md, 0.65rem);
  }

  .prps__principle-mark {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    color: var(--prps-accent);
    font-weight: 800;
  }

  .prps__principle p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--prps-text-secondary);
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm, 0.875rem);
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .prps__principle strong {
    color: var(--prps-text);
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .prps__questions,
    .prps__cards {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .prps__question--wide {
      grid-column: auto;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .prps {
      padding: 1rem;
    }

    .prps__header,
    .prps__result-head {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 0.75rem;
    }

    .prps__badge {
      align-self: flex-start;
    }

    .prps__result-level {
      text-align: left;
    }
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .prps__meter span,
    .prps__options label span {
      transition: none;
    }
  }
</style>
